    "body": "fix on issue/1102-lathe-body-signed-reach · PR #1167 · pinned by operation::turning_holder_side::tests::{the_side_is_where_the_path_reaches_and_a_past_centre_overrun_keeps_it, a_rear_tool_past_centre_is_read_on_its_own_side_like_its_front_mirror} · merges when reviewed. Finding: every turning generator emits tips at rho >= 0 in its own half plane, so no generated path carries X < 0 today (latent, stays P2). The law now reads the body on the holder's per-path side, and a path on both sides beyond a 2.5 mm past-centre overrun is refused by name.",
